cff-version: 1.2.0
title: pdfnative-mcp
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: Nizoka
    website: "https://github.com/Nizoka"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nizoka/pdfnative-mcp"
url: "https://github.com/Nizoka/pdfnative-mcp"
abstract: >-
  Model Context Protocol (MCP) server bridging the zero-dependency pdfnative
  library to AI clients. Provides 28 production-grade tools for PDF generation
  (13 document block kinds, page layout options, a read-only pagination preview),
  PDF/A archival with embedded fonts and conformance diagnostics, PDF/UA
  structural validation, native vector charts, embedded barcodes, multi-script
  text, smart tables, interactive forms (create, read, fill, flatten), embedded
  files (Factur-X), digital signatures with the full PAdES long-term-validation
  ladder (B-B to B-LTA: RFC 3161 timestamps, DSS, document timestamps) and
  verification, print production (page boxes, bleed, printer's marks), document
  metadata updates, encryption round-trip, page-tree operations, markup
  annotations, Unicode text extraction, PDF introspection, and human-in-the-loop
  governance issue drafting. Speaks MCP 2026-07-28 with automatic fallback for
  2025-era clients and makes no outbound network call by default.
license: MIT
version: 1.6.0
date-released: "2026-08-23"
